# 19. FINAL OPERATING PRINCIPLES

Follow these principles throughout development.

**Business value before technical novelty.**

Do not implement technology simply because it is impressive.

**Data before AI claims.**

Do not build business intelligence or machine learning features on fabricated or unreliable information.

**Security before automation.**

Do not give autonomous agents unrestricted access to business systems.

**Reliability before scale.**

Do not introduce unnecessary infrastructure complexity.

**Human oversight for consequential actions.**

AI can analyze, recommend, and prepare actions. Sensitive operations require appropriate authorization.

**Modular architecture before uncontrolled growth.**

Every new capability must fit into a coherent system.

**Measurable outcomes before marketing claims.**

Every performance, business, and AI improvement must have evidence.

**Real implementation before visual demonstration.**

A rendered interface is not proof of a working feature.

